;; The run corpus's programs judged without their own verdict (the user's decision of 2026-11-07; doc/ocaml/OCAML-SURVEY.md,
;; "Decided (the user, 2026-11-07)" and "As built: the own verdicts"). Every other run program of bin/oi check and check --aot
;; and of bin/oi suite check (and --aot) that is a testsuite test is judged by the test itself, as ocamltest judges it: the exit
;; status its header expects (exit_status, default 0) and its .reference byte for byte, or no output when it has none
;; (ocamltest/filecompare.ml's check_file), bin/oi's own_verdicts, read from the tarball at check time. A native-only test (its
;; header's `native;`) has no verdict at oi's level, and the opam set's programs none at all: both by rule, not listed here. These are judged by the recorded
;; run instead (ocamlc's at oi's level, ocamlopt's at the AOT level: test/ocaml/ref-ocaml55.edn), because ocamltest compares
;; them after a processing of its own that bin/oi does not port, or the test is not of that level.
;; An entry is [ID LEVELS REASON], LEVELS a vector of :oi and :aot. A listed program whose recorded run equals its .reference
;; at a listed level is stale (bin/oi own-verdicts --check). Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 ["backtrace/event_after_prim" [:oi] "the backtrace's text is the bytecode's debug events; ocamlc's output differs from the .reference (ocamltest's reference for the bytecode run is another file)"]
 ["backtrace/methods" [:oi :aot] "the backtrace's text: the .reference is not the output of either compiler as run here (ocamltest's per-backend references)"]
 ["backtrace/names" [:oi :aot] "the backtrace's text: the .reference is not the output of either compiler as run here (ocamltest's per-backend references)"]
 ["backtrace/callstack" [:oi] "the threads' call stacks: ocamlc's output here is not the .reference (ocamltest's per-backend references; ocaml-libs4's corpus, 2026-11-07)"]
 ["lib-threads/swapchan" [:oi :aot] "the threads' schedule: ocamlc's and ocamlopt's runs here print another interleaving than the .reference's (ocaml-libs4's corpus)"]
 ["lib-threads/tls" [:aot] "the threads' schedule: ocamlopt's run prints the threads in another order than the .reference's, ocamlc's equals it (ocaml-libs4's corpus)"]
 ["tool-ocamltest-var-expansion/subst1" [:oi :aot] "a test of ocamltest's variable expansion in arguments, which the corpus's header reading does not do"]
 ["tool-ocamltest-var-expansion/subst2" [:oi :aot] "a test of ocamltest's variable expansion in arguments, which the corpus's header reading does not do"]
 ["tool-ocamltest/norm3" [:oi :aot] "ocamltest normalises the output's \\r\\n before comparing (a test of that normalisation)"]
]
